From 5db0d0902a1267d4ab31a3bd8c8ddda6c08dd62d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravikanth Tuniki <ravikanth.tuniki@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 11 Sep 2025 10:52:51 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 108/110] net: axienet: Replace MRMAC GT memory-mapped
 registers with GPIO controls

Replace the memory-mapped register approach for MRMAC GT (Gigabit
Transceiver) control with GPIO-based controls.

In existing Design, Reset GPIO pins for all lanes are concatenated
and connected to MRMAC IP, requiring synchronized reset for all
lanes.

With New GT Wizard Design on 2025.1 and above, individual reset GPIO
pins per lane connected directly to GT, enabling per-lane reset control.

This refactoring ensures proper reset coordination between multiple
MRMAC lanes while maintaining backward compatibility with existing
designs and enabling support for new designs.

Signed-off-by: Ravikanth Tuniki <ravikanth.tuniki@amd.com>
Reviewed-by: Harini Katakam <harini.katakam@amd.com>
Message-ID: <20250911052251.10925-5-ravikanth.tuniki@amd.com>
